# Line-ending policy (issue #11).
#
# `text=auto` makes LF-in-the-index a property of the REPOSITORY rather than of
# each contributor's `core.autocrlf`. It deliberately does NOT set `eol`, so the
# working tree keeps whatever the platform's git produces -- CRLF on a default
# Windows checkout, LF elsewhere. Adding it caused zero churn: every tracked
# file was already LF in the index (`git ls-files --eol` reports no `i/crlf` and
# no `i/mixed`), so no renormalise commit was needed.
#
# It is the guard for the other half of #11: `endOfLine: "auto"` in
# .prettierrc.json makes `ui:format:check` accept a native-CRLF working tree --
# which it must, or `npm run ui:check` is unusable on Windows and never reaches
# the test suites -- but that also means prettier would no longer object to a
# CRLF file being committed. This line keeps that from happening at the layer
# where it actually matters.
#
# A repo-wide `eol=lf` would ALSO fix the prettier symptom, by forcing LF into
# every working tree. Not done: it rewrites every existing checkout, overrides a
# setting contributors are entitled to choose, and buys nothing the pair above
# does not already deliver.
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRECEDENCE: git resolves .gitattributes by LAST MATCHING LINE, not by most
# specific pattern (gitattributes(5): "If multiple patterns match the path, a
# later line overrides an earlier line"). The entries below win over `* text=auto`
# because they come AFTER it. Anything appended below them overrides THEM --
# so a new wildcard added at the bottom would silently un-protect the
# byte-compared assets these lines exist to protect. Append above this block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generated frontend bundle. Its committed bytes are compared against a fresh
# build by CI, and that check is a PAIR (.github/workflows/ci.yml):
#
#     npm run ui:build
#     git diff --exit-code -- crates/alms-gateway/static/ui-dist
#     test -z "$(git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all -- ...)"
#
# The first condition applies git's clean filter, so a CRLF working tree is
# invisible to it; the second does not, and reports every generated file whose
# working-tree line endings differ from what the build just wrote. Under
# `* text=auto` alone, a Windows checkout materialises the multi-line chunks as
# CRLF while vite writes LF, so the second condition fails locally and CI --
# being Linux, and therefore LF -- never sees it. The drift gate was not
# reproducible off Linux.
#
# `eol=lf` here fixes that at the checkout layer. The objections to a repo-wide
# `eol=lf` do not apply to this directory: nobody hand-edits a minified bundle,
# and byte-identity with a fresh build is the entire point of committing it.
crates/alms-gateway/static/ui-dist/** text eol=lf

# Source template for the bundle above; hashed asset names are injected into it
# at build time, so it is compared the same way and needs the same treatment.
crates/alms-gateway/static/ui/index.html text eol=lf
